    "rich_text_p7D8ce": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "spacer_L8mYri": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "heading_MrGjAB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Your Floating Candle Questions",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "text_phgQQw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Below,  we address all your queries around floating candles. </p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_6THxWy": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the difference between your 1.75-inch and 3-inch floating candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 1.75-inch floating candles for smaller bowls, grouped centerpieces, and tighter table layouts, and choose 3-inch floating candles when you want a fuller candle presence in larger bowls, vases, or statement arrangements. At Kisco Candles, we carry both sizes in classic round shapes so you can scale the look without changing the overall style.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ykeVbb": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which floating candle color should I choose?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose white floating candles for a brighter, cleaner look and ivory for a softer, warmer finish. Both colors work well for weddings, dinners, and home décor, so the better choice usually depends on the tone of your florals, linens, and glassware.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_68L9WH": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What pack size should I buy for floating candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose a 20-pack or 12-pack when you are styling a smaller setup, and choose a 40-pack or 24-pack when you are decorating more tables or filling more vessels. Our smaller packs make sense for occasional home use and mockups, while the larger packs are a stronger fit for events and venue work. You can also order these candles in bulk if you need more.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_zbiA3h": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_YnWqLz": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What containers work best with floating candles?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_HcQMNY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Use clear glass bowls, cylinder vases, shallow bowls, or water-filled trays for the cleanest floating candle display. These candles are especially effective in glass because the flame reflects off the water and the vessel, which gives the arrangement more depth without adding visual clutter.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_7QXgMW": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_pFWUib": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are your floating candles unscented?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_n6pNpj": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, our floating candles are designed for a clean ambiance without adding fragrance to the room. That makes them a practical choice for dining tables, weddings, and events where scent can compete with food, florals, or the feel of the space.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_NfQGVQ": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_cxD4QA": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I use floating candles outdoors?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_yHXzGk": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, floating candles work beautifully outdoors in pools, ponds, and open-air water features. For the steadiest flame, place them in calm water and avoid exposed spots where strong wind can disturb the surface.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_ignrJA": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_mWKARb": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which floating candles work best for wedding centerpieces?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_XYidLt": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 1.75-inch floating candles when you are using many smaller centerpieces, and choose 3-inch floating candles when each table has one larger vessel or a more dramatic focal arrangement. White is the cleaner match for bright wedding palettes, and ivory blends more softly with warm-toned flowers and candlelight-heavy rooms.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_Wnx6QU": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_K8EeNU": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How do I get the cleanest look from a floating candle arrangement?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_6jKypU": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Fill the vessel with clean water, keep the surface still, and leave enough open space around each candle so it can float evenly. A simple setup with clear glass, fresh water, and the same size candles per vessel usually looks the most polished.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_MeV6Fw": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "subheading_cCeUPE": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How many floating candles should I order for an event?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_rLLBN7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Order by vessel count first, then choose the pack size that gets you close to the final number with a small backup cushion. If you are using one candle per bowl across many tables, the 40-pack 1.75-inch option or the 24-pack 3-inch option can save time compared with buying several smaller packs.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        }
      },
